speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I wish to thank the hon. members and I think that the minister is even more magnanimous than those back-benchers who said that I should speak for a few minutes only. However, I shall not take too much of the time of the house to conclude my remarks.
The Quebec taxpayers, because they do not contribute to the federal government medicare program any more than those of some other provinces at present will have to pay taxes to help its cost. I do not suggest that this program is a bad thing, but the federal government, before putting it into force, should first have consulted the provinces so as to establish a plan meeting the conditions laid down by the provinces.
[English}
